From: Sergio Martin
Subject: [PATCH] chimera: a clipped noperspective value is measured on the screen axis where the ends are furthest apart

When the clipper makes a new vertex, it works out how far along the edge
the vertex is on the screen, for the values a shader asked to be
interpolated without perspective. It measured that along x whenever the two
ends' x before the divide by W differed, even when their x on the screen
was nearly the same: for an edge running up the screen to a vertex behind
the eye, the factor was one tiny difference over another, and the new
vertex's values were wrong. Supermodel's New3D draws four-cornered polygons
with such values, and a floor reaching behind the camera came out smeared
(Chimera issue 479: vf3's subway floor, Scud Race's road). The axis is now
the one on which the ends are furthest apart on the screen.
---
diff -ru a/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_pipe_clip.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_pipe_clip.c
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_pipe_clip.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_pipe_clip.c
@@ -191,15 +191,23 @@
     */
    if (clip->num_linear_attribs) {
       float t_nopersp = t;
-      /* find either in.x != out.x or in.y != out.y */
+      /* Chimera: measured on the screen axis on which the two ends are
+       * furthest apart. Upstream took x whenever the ends' x before the
+       * divide by W differed, even when their x on the screen was nearly
+       * the same (an edge running up the screen to a vertex behind the
+       * eye): the factor was then one tiny difference over another, and
+       * the new vertex's values were wrong (Supermodel's floors near the
+       * camera came out smeared, Chimera issue 479). */
+      float apart = 0.0f;
       for (int k = 0; k < 2; k++) {
-         if (in->clip_pos[k] != out->clip_pos[k]) {
-            /* do divide by W, then compute linear interpolation factor */
-            float in_coord = in->clip_pos[k] / in->clip_pos[3];
-            float out_coord = out->clip_pos[k] / out->clip_pos[3];
-            float dst_coord = dst->clip_pos[k] / dst->clip_pos[3];
+         /* do divide by W, then compute linear interpolation factor */
+         float in_coord = in->clip_pos[k] / in->clip_pos[3];
+         float out_coord = out->clip_pos[k] / out->clip_pos[3];
+         float dst_coord = dst->clip_pos[k] / dst->clip_pos[3];
+         float d = fabsf(in_coord - out_coord);
+         if (d > apart && isfinite(d)) {
+            apart = d;
             t_nopersp = (dst_coord - out_coord) / (in_coord - out_coord);
-            break;
          }
       }
       for (unsigned j = 0; j < clip->num_linear_attribs; j++) {
